<section class="wrap feature-duo"><figure><a href="screenshots.php" aria-label="See Calculator in the screenshot gallery"><?php screenshot_image('calculator.png'); ?></a><figcaption>Arithmetic, directly in the launcher.</figcaption></figure><div><p class="eyebrow">YOUR SETUP, YOUR CHOICE</p><h2>Start small.<br>Add what you use.</h2><p>Calculator, Clock, Memory, File Finder, System Commands, and Assigns and Volumes start enabled. Switch on the other tools in Preferences when you need them.</p><p>Use applies settings for the session; Save keeps them. Plugin settings have their own Save and Cancel window, with Browse for known executable and drawer paths. Calculator also converts units and C/F/K temperatures offline. Restore defaults stages the original values until you save, so you can try a reset and still cancel it.</p></div></section>
<section class="wrap section faq-section" id="faq"><div class="faq-heading"><p class="eyebrow">HELP &amp; GETTING STARTED</p><h2>A few answers.</h2></div><div class="faq-list">
<details><summary>How do I install it?</summary><p>Unpack the LHA and open Install. Novice handles the standard setup; Intermediate and Expert let you choose the destination and autostart. All bundled packages are installed, with only six essential local plugins enabled. The installer starts Beam68 in the background and shows your configured shortcut.</p></details>
<details><summary>What does it need?</summary><p>AmigaOS 3.0 or later and a 68000 or later CPU. AmigaOS 3.2 and a 68020 are recommended. Memory use depends on your index. Optional plugins need their corresponding applications or network tools. See <a href="source.php#compatibility">compatibility notes</a>.</p></details>
<details><summary>Can I recall previous plugin searches?</summary><p>Yes. F7 and Shift+F7 recall read-only searches for the current bundled plugin, separately from application history. Each plugin keeps up to 12 entries. Recall fills the search field; actions such as downloads, playback and device control are excluded.</p></details>
<details><summary>Can I update without losing settings?</summary><p>Yes. Updates retain saved choices. Uninstall lets you keep or remove settings, including temporary preferences when removing them.</p></details>
<details><summary>Does it access the network automatically?</summary><p>All network plugins start disabled on a fresh installation. Enable Aminet Browser, Wikipedia or AmiHASS in Preferences when needed. Aminet asks before downloading; Wikipedia requires curl with working HTTPS support.</p></details>
<details><summary>Can I add plugins or change the theme?</summary><p>Import plugins in Preferences. All themes are editable and can be restored to their original palette. The <a href="developers.php">Developers page</a> covers the plugin SDK and theme format; <a href="source.php">Source</a> explains building the app.</p></details>
<details><summary>How do I choose which drawers are searched?</summary><p>Open Preferences → Indexing and add the drawers you want. Set file patterns, exclusions and a finite depth, or select Unlimited to include all reachable directory levels. WHDLoad shares these settings when enabled.</p></details>
<details><summary>What are Favorites and Application shortcuts?</summary><p>Favorites pins frequently used programs and read-only plugin queries, and supports groups such as <code>fav:games</code>. Press F6 on a result or read-only plugin query to pin or unpin it. Opening a saved query fills the launcher without running it. Application shortcuts adds extra search words and custom named launch actions to individual programs.</p></details>
<details><summary>What is the difference between Use and Save?</summary><p>Both apply changes to the running launcher. Use keeps the main configuration for the current session; Save also preserves it across restarts. Preferences waits for confirmation before closing. Individual plugin settings have their own Save and Cancel window.</p></details>
<details><summary>Does Escape quit Beam68?</summary><p>Escape hides the search window while Beam68 stays resident. Press your configured shortcut to show it again. The default is Ctrl + Alt + Space. F4 quits the launcher.</p></details>
<details><summary>Can I change the global shortcut?</summary><p>Yes. Use the hotkey controls in Preferences → General. The installer displays your configured keys after installation or update, including a shortcut retained from saved settings.</p></details>
<details><summary>Does Aminet Browser install packages for me?</summary><p>It searches, shows package information and asks before downloading. Completion offers Open drawer, View readme and Install. Its installation action checks the archive signature and opens the archive with your archive handler. Failed downloads clean up partial data and offer an explicit retry. View readme uses MultiView. Opening a downloaded drawer or archive requires workbench.library V44+; archives also need a suitable handler. Follow the package’s own installer or instructions; Beam68 does not automatically install its contents.</p></details>
<details><summary>Can I reset a theme after editing it?</summary><p>Yes. Choose the theme in Appearance and use Restore original palette. Each theme has its own saved colours, so restoring one does not reset the others. Mocha is the default; Rose is the reddish built-in palette.</p></details>
<details><summary>Can I remove bundled plugins?</summary><p>Bundled plugins can be disabled with Toggle, but Remove is unavailable for them. Additional third-party plugins can be imported and removed in Preferences. Priority up and down change their ordering.</p></details>
<details><summary>Can I use Home Assistant from Beam68?</summary><p>Enable the optional AmiHASS plugin after installing, configuring and starting the AmiHASS service. Search entities and read states with <code>ha:kitchen</code>. Supported device actions require confirmation. Beam68 reuses the service’s connection and keeps no separate Home Assistant token. Use a current service with working catalogue support.</p></details>
<details><summary>What happens if a plugin is slow or unavailable?</summary><p>Beam68 shows Searching or Working while a request runs, distinguishes no matches from errors, and offers Retry for supported read-only queries. Typing remains available, old-query replies are ignored, and refreshing results keeps the selected item when it is still present. Use <code>health:</code> to inspect plugin outcomes.</p></details>
<details><summary>Can I stop an index scan?</summary><p>The launcher shows the current drawer, scanned entries and indexed items. Its progress bar counts completed roots. Click the banner to cancel, or check counters with <code>scan:status</code>. Press Ctrl+F2 or use <code>scan:cancel</code> to stop scanning while retaining existing results. <code>scan:failures</code> lists recent failed locations and lets you retry their scan roots.</p></details>
<details><summary>Can I restore a plugin’s settings?</summary><p>For plugins with settings, open Settings and choose Restore defaults. The values remain pending until Save; Cancel discards the edits and leaves the saved file alone.</p></details>
<details><summary>What happens when I import a plugin?</summary><p>Preferences shows the package identity, version and file inventory before copying it. New imports start disabled; updates retain their activation choice. Bundled plugins are updated with Beam68. Import code from sources you trust: native plugins run with your access.</p></details>
<details><summary>How do result actions work?</summary><p>Tab, right-click or the result footer opens applicable actions. Use Up/Down and Enter, click an action, or press its number. Escape closes the menu without hiding Beam68. The footer describes what Enter will do.</p></details>
<details><summary>Can results show their locations?</summary><p>Appearance → Window layout → Two-line rows shows names above locations or descriptions. Disable it for compact columns. Short and compact displays automatically use single-line rows.</p></details>
<details><summary>Does Beam68 record my clipboard?</summary><p>Recording is off by default. Enable Clipboard Tools, then explicitly run <code>clip:history on</code> to record future text changes for this session. Entry, retained-text and expiry limits are configurable. <code>clip:history off</code> stops and clears recording. History stays on RAM: and is not saved to preferences; text over 120 bytes is skipped.</p></details>
<details><summary>How can I check a plugin’s dependencies?</summary><p>Plugin Details shows local readiness for supported integrations and offers Check readiness. AmiHASS has an explicit read-only Test connection. These checks do not enable plugins, start services or operate devices.</p></details>
<details><summary>Where can I find help or build my own plugin?</summary><p>Press F1 in Beam68 for command help, or read the included AmigaGuide. The <a href="developers.php">Developers page</a> links to the plugin SDK, examples and theme format. Visit <a href="source.php">Source</a> for app build instructions. Beam68 and its SDK use the MIT licence.</p></details>
      <details><summary>How do plugin RAM copies and cancelled searches behave?</summary><p>Optional RAM copies are checked against the complete source package before reuse, including helper files. Unfinished requests retain bounded slots after cancellation; late replies do not replace newer results. If an indexed volume is disconnected, reconnect it and press F2 to rescan.</p></details>
</div></section>
